  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">OUTPUT A: Exchanging best practices on Port State Control (PSC) and the development of a constructive dialogue between experts on enforcement of safety regulation, which improves maritime safety</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="271006" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activities on PSC to exchange methods and knowledge</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Three joint activities during the project period with focus on best practices within PSC resulting in a short written report with recommendations and/or potential areas for future cooperation on enforcement of safety regulation between DMA and China MSA

Flag inspection done onboard a Chinese flagged ship in a Chinese harbour"></target>
     <actual value="A visit by Danish Maritime Accident Investigation Board to MSA in China took place 28 October - 2 November 2023. Besides participating in a workshop with MSA 31 October in Shanghai, DMAIB representatives held meetings with Maersk Asia-Pacific office and Shanghai Maritime University to get a company as well as an academic perspective on various issues related to marine accidents."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Activities on PSC to exchange methods and knowledge"></target>
     <actual value="Activities postponed to 2021 and 2022 due to COVID19. Activities will only be carried out on location. Implementation awaiting confirmation from MSA."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Activities on PSC to exchange methods and knowledge"></target>
     <actual value="The COVID19 situation in China continued to severely influence the execution of the planned activities in 2022 under Phase II of the SSC. However, several of the planned activities were successfully implemented as on-line meetings and webinars, including important activities relating to the green transition of the global maritime sector."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Activities on PSC to exchange methods and knowledge"></target>
     <actual value="The COVID19-pandemic and the related travel restrictions made it impossible to implement the planned Port State Control activities. The possibility of organising webinars was discussed, but DMA and MSA agreed that a webinar would be of only limited value to the participants. Thus, the PSC activities have been postponed to 2022 pending the travel restrictions and quarantine requirements in China to be removed."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">OUTPUT B: Optimization of routing leading to more sustainable shipping routes and the reduction of navigational errors, which can cause groundings and other casualties.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="271007" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seminar on Ships Routing and Reporting Systems with a focus on optimizing routing and reduce risk of navigational errors and accidents.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Workshop on Ships Routing and Reporting System"></target>
     <actual value="DMA and MSA held a webinar 16 September 2022 on safety on board offshore vessels and safety of navigation related issues in light of continuous expansion of offshore windfarms"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Seminar on Ships Routing and Reporting Systems with a focus on optimizing routing and reduce risk of navigational errors and accidents."></target>
     <actual value="TBC in 2021 in Denmark or webinar"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Seminar on Ships Routing and Reporting Systems with a focus on optimizing routing and reduce risk of navigational errors and accidents."></target>
     <actual value="The COVID19-pandemic and the related travel restrictions made it impossible to implement most of the planned activities. On 25 November 2021, the DMA and MSA held a webinar on digital certificates for seafarers and digital ship certificates. The rest of the scheduled activities have been postponed to 2022 or until the travel situation is back to normal."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Workshop on Ships Routing and Reporting System"></target>
     <actual value="Visit to Denmark by MSA delegation planned for August 2023 has been postponed and is expected to be organised end June 2024."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">OUTPUT C: Improved implementation of the goals in China&#x2019;s 14th Five-Year Plan (2021-2025), related to the improvement of the marine environment and reducing emissions from shipping</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="275864" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Not applicable as baseline, impact indicators are not defined for current SSC projects.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Improved implementation of the goals in China&#x2019;s 14th Five-Year Plan (2021-2025), related to the improvement of the marine environment and reducing emissions from shipping"></target>
     <actual value="The positive dialogue between Denmark and China concerning IMO measures to reduce GHG emissions continued in 2021, and the dialogue on IMO measures will continue and developed further in 2022. A successful webinar with MSA on maritime GHG reduction was held on 10 May 2021 and follow up activities with MSA/MOT and their subordinated research institutes are due to be implemented in 2022, including a follow-up webinar with MSA. Moreover, at the Second UN Global Conference on Sustainable Transport Conference in Beijing 14-16 October 2021 Minister For Industry, Business and Financial Affairs Simon Kollerup held an on-line speech focusing on Green Shipping. Finally, a very successful webinar with MIIT was organized in December 2021 under the overall theme &#x201c;the path towards Maritime Decarbonization and Zero Emissions Ships &#x2013; Future Cooperation opportunities&#x201d;."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Improved implementation of the goals in China&#x2019;s 14th Five-Year Plan (2021-2025), related to the improvement of the marine environment and reducing emissions from shipping"></target>
     <actual value="Two additional webinars with MSA were organised 1 June and 4 November 2022."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Improved implementation of the goals in China&#x2019;s 14th Five-Year Plan (2021-2025), related to the improvement of the marine environment and reducing emissions from shipping"></target>
     <actual value="Two webinars with MSA will was held 13 April and 2 June 2023 i.e. in advance of the important IMO MEPC80 meeting in July 2023 at which the new ambitious IMO GHG 2023 strategy was adopted."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
